Even with the standard deduction, you can take "above-the-line" deductions and business deductions:
*   **Student Loan Interest:** You paid $4,800, but the IRS caps the student loan interest deduction at **$2,500** per return. Because your combined Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) is around $89,700, you are well below the 2024 phase-out limits for MFJ ($165,000–$195,000). You can deduct the maximum $2,500 as an adjustment to income.
*   **Work Supplies ($780):** 
